description:Pokémon Identifier & Stats Viewer
Project Overview
Build an image recognition system that identifies Pokémon species from uploaded images and displays their detailed stats and information.
Tech Stack Integration
Cursor IDE: Primary development environment
Python: Core programming language with ML libraries
PostgreSQL: Store Pokémon stats data and classification results
Git/GitHub: Version control and collaboration
Key Libraries: TensorFlow/Keras, OpenCV, FastAPI, SQLAlchemy
Project Goals
Develop a CNN model to classify Pokémon species from images
Create a database with comprehensive Pokémon stats and information
Build REST API for image classification and stats retrieval
Design a web interface for image upload and stats display
Store classification history in PostgreSQL
Core Features
Pokémon Image Classification: Upload image and identify Pokémon species (20-50 different species)
Stats Display: Show detailed Pokémon information including:
Base stats (HP, Attack, Defense, Speed, Special Attack, Special Defense)
Type(s) and type effectiveness
Height, weight, and abilities
Generation and Pokédex number
Classification History: Track previous identifications and results
Confidence Scoring: Display prediction confidence for each classification
Search by Name: Alternative way to look up Pokémon stats
Technical Requirements
Python 3.8+ with ML libraries (TensorFlow, OpenCV, Pillow, NumPy)
PostgreSQL database for Pokémon stats and classification logs
FastAPI for REST API development
Basic web technologies (HTML/CSS/JavaScript) for user interface
Pokémon image dataset and stats data
Success Metrics
Model Performance: >90% accuracy on Pokémon classification
Database Integration: Complete Pokémon stats database with proper relationships
User Experience: Smooth image upload with immediate stats display
API Functionality: Working endpoints for classification and stats retrieval
Documentation: Clear setup instructions and usage guide
Learning Outcomes
Practical experience with image classification and CNN models
Database design for structured data storage and retrieval
REST API development and integration
Frontend development for ML applications
Data preprocessing and model training workflows
Version control and project documentation
Deliverables
Trained Pokémon classification model
PostgreSQL database with complete Pokémon stats
REST API with classification and stats endpoints
Web interface for image upload and stats viewing
Classification history tracking system
Complete project documentation and demo
Data Resources
Images: Kaggle Pokémon Images Dataset (https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/vishalsubbiah/pokemon-images-and-types)
Stats Data: PokéAPI (https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/) for comprehensive Pokémon information
Backup Data: GitHub Pokémon CSV datasets for offline access
